From 43a858090697035a57dbf8f4e3ad14b25fd38723 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CanMehEvolve <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Profile::GetMesg: table of pointers instead of indices

What: the lookup table stores const MESG* directly (zero-initialised static), dropping the 0xFFFF fill loop and the index dereference.
Why it might be faster: one fewer step per lookup and a cheaper first call. Step measured 0.12%, within noise. Same thread-safety caveat as the earlier GetMesg change.

Provenance: greedy search, seed 3, generation 34, region 574 (Profile::GetMesg).
Generated by the model (deepseek-v4.1-flash); not hand-written. Search-time ratio R (candidate/stock, <1 is faster): 0.8576 -> 0.8565 at acceptance (max of two measurements). This is a ranking value, NOT an independent per-patch
confirmation; only the fixed FINAL patch of the run was re-measured independently.
Cumulative patch it was derived from: runs/deepseek/greedy-s3-1072869/patches/gen_34.patch (diff against stock; do not apply together with the others).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fit_profile.cpp | 15 ++++-----------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fit_profile.cpp b/src/fit_profile.cpp
index a9973fa..3bd2a02 100644
--- a/src/fit_profile.cpp
+++ b/src/fit_profile.cpp
@@ -3057,29 +3057,22 @@ const Profile::MESG Profile::mesgs[MESGS] =
 
 const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
 {
-    static FIT_UINT16 lookup[65536];
+    static const MESG* lookup[65536];
     static bool initialized = false;
 
     if (!initialized)
     {
-        for (int i = 0; i < 65536; ++i)
-            lookup[i] = 0xFFFF;
-
         for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
         {
             const FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
-            if (lookup[n] == 0xFFFF)
-                lookup[n] = static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(i);
+            if (lookup[n] == NULL)
+                lookup[n] = &mesgs[i];
         }
 
         initialized = true;
     }
 
-    const FIT_UINT16 idx = lookup[num];
-    if (idx == 0xFFFF)
-        return NULL;
-
-    return &mesgs[idx];
+    return lookup[num];
 }
 
 const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const std::string& name)
